       "description": "Reference: the same cold-season run and the same real64 kernels/noah_driver, replayed at ESM_DT = 1e-6 s, at rel 1e-9. THE POINT OF THIS REGIME is that it is exactly where a naively written compaction component fails: the density increment is 7.5e-17 of the density, so both sndens_out - sndens_in and sndens (pexp - 1) return pure round-off, and only the cancellation-free form -- sndens_in pexp_m1 + dw (1 - dsx), referenced against the series sum published before WRF adds one to it -- still carries the signal. `dsndens_dt` is the dt -> 0 compaction rate here to twelve digits. Step 392 of case D, a trace pack over frozen ground in a dry column. SNOWPACK's melt-water retention branch RUNS -- the snow surface is at or above freezing; the pack is below the esdcx floor, so the compaction argument uses the floored 0.01 cm while the depth diagnostic keeps the true water equivalent; neither density limit fires. The dt -> 0 compaction rate is 6.9998e-11 per second, and the 60 s regime's tendency for the same step exceeds it by xarg/3 = 1.32e-08 relative.",
